The irony here is profound.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:23.320
You have states like California desperately grasping for new untested

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:26.800
revenue streams to fund basic social safety nets.

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:32.000
They're trying to tax theoretical tech wealth, unrealized gains at the exact

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:36.000
moment that wealth is being exposed as an AI driven illusion or at least

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:37.080
highly overvalued.

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:37.880
Exactly.

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:42.000
The tech sector, which was supposed to be this infinite money engine, is

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:45.360
faltering under the crushing weight of investor expectations and physical

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:46.560
infrastructure costs.

00:14:46.680 --> 00:14:50.600
And at the exact same time, the legacy manufacturing base that actually built

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:54.560
the 20th century middle class is collapsing under the pressure of new

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:58.640
global competition from China and geopolitical instability in places like

00:14:58.640 --> 00:14:59.560
the Strait of Hormuz.

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:00.360
Exactly.

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:04.360
Every major pillar of the global economy is shifting simultaneously.

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:09.280
The friction between extreme wealth, the billions generated by tech and the

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:13.560
actual economic reality of building physical things and moving them across

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:16.080
oceans is currently dominating the globe.

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:20.360
It's an economy searching for stable footing and finding absolute volatility

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:20.840
instead.

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:24.760
And for you listening, these aren't isolated events happening in a vacuum

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:28.120
or in a textbook, whether you're looking at the cost of your health care

